      "after_tool_count": 34,
      "text": "Found one substantive, well-supported discrepancy: **F1:W4** (south wall, small window) is currently modeled with the same height/position as the standard windows (sill 1.007m, head 2.605m, height 1.60m), but pixel measurement against the South elevation — cross-validated against the door and large windows, which match the candidate almost exactly — shows this window is actually much smaller and set higher: sill ≈1.51m, head ≈2.10m, height ≈0.59m (width/position already match well). Let me record this as a claim and revise it."
